From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:38:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 204/307] feat: three-cascade LPV LOD chain + RSM depth
 re-encoding + SH de-ringing

Root-cause fixes (investigations/gi_lpv/10, 11):
- RSM depth encoding: the depth buffer stores LINEAR (Z-n)/(F-n) while
  the projective inverse expects z_ndc - the mismatch stretched all
  content along the sun axis proportionally to the depth range
  (~17-35 m at r_LPVRsmClipRange 700; user-diagnosed). Every consumer
  (inject, resolve sky test, debug 8) now converts via LPVRsmDepthRange
  pinned with the matrices. The caster-collection sweep also follows the
  clip range so near/far occlusion honesty matches.
- SH L1 ringing: a pure cosine lobe evaluates negative against an
  opposing receiver and ate the co-stored ambient (black discs around
  sun patches). LPVEvalReceiver scales only the negative directional
  term by 0.25 = A0^2/A1^2 - pure lobe lands at exactly zero, aligned
  response and wall-leak cancellation unchanged.

Cascade LOD chain (user design):
- MaxCascadeNum 3, r_LPVCascadeScale is now the PER STEP ratio
  (default 3: 96 / 288 / 864 m), RSM resolution halves per cascade
  (1024 / 512 / 256), chained blend weights with a 30% fade band,
  far-cascade iteration halving removed (energy consistency at seams).
- Height map AO damps the coarse cascades indoors
  (r_LPVHeightMapOcclusion): their 6 / 18 m cells cannot resolve walls.
- Guards: cache-lod reservation underflow (enabling height map AO
  poisoned nCachedLodCount and killed the sun shadows), RSM MRT size
  mismatch during level switches drops the pass for one frame.
- Debug 13 / 14 / 15: mid raw / near-vs-mid energy compare / outer raw.
- Defaults from the user's three-scene sweet spot: bounce 0.15,
  sky 0.15, MaxIrradiance 3, Occlusion 10.

